{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1398422-1001-demon-the-descent-antagonists","id":1398422,"title":"1001 Demon the Descent Antagonists","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-23T13:26:05-07:00","id":1398422,"title":"1001 Demon the Descent Antagonists","content":"Thought I'd create a post about generating Demon antagonists for inspiration. Feel free to add to the list.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><u><b>The Wanna Be Immortal</b></u> - Immortality is a difficult thing to come by. This person wishes for such power. They have heard of Demons and is hoping to find one to get their wish. No crime is too heinous, no price to high. At least one Demon has crossed their path, noting that such a person is a danger to not only themselves, but the world as well.</li> <li><b><u>The Demon of Destruction</u></b> - This Demon was given the task to destroy entire cities as an Angel. One day it did too good a job and fell. Now it resides in an old folks home, in what it considers &quot;retirement&quot;. But it knows that Angles and Demons might locate it. Looking for information or possibly to bend it to another's will. Angels report back to the God-Machine and Demons talk. The Demon of Destruction still prides itself on being a Destroyer at heart and will try to make sure no one can report on its existence. Urban legend surrounds the Demon of Destruction, many a Demon Ring and Agency has gone dark after accidentally entering its territory.</li> <li><b><u>Dr. Fletcher</u></b> - The owner of a Blood Bank in the area. Dr. Fletcher is never seen during the day. He tends to keep to himself. In the last few months blood has entered the bank that is of a distinct quality. Apparently a Demon had been staking out the place for marks and donated blood without thinking. Now the Vampire Dr. Fletcher has had a taste for Demon blood and wants more.</li> </ol><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T11:58:43-07:00","id":1398835,"title":"","content":"4. <u><b>Jess Clark </b></u>- Jess's young adult son, Mike, turned his life around. He stopped doing drugs, went to college, was dating a nice guy. But then he changed. The doctors called it a fugue state, but she suspected an unholy cause. Mike dropped out of college, left his girlfriend, and soon cut ties almost completely. In researching, a book fell into her lap that detailed the signs of Demonic possession. As she researched she began to see his Cover glitch though to her they were signs of the devil. She managed to track down Mike, and kill him in his sleep. No holy water, no magic ritual. She took her skills and began cultivating a group of people who had similar experiences, teaching how to see the signs of Demonic Possession and to kill the demon while its vulnerable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T13:45:34-07:00","id":1398867,"title":"","content":"5. <u><b>Dr. Perdition</b></u> - Dr. Susan Smith was a surgeon in a prestigious hospital One day she had a gunshot victim under the knife. When she opened him up she didn't see what she should have. Instead she saw was Infrastructure. The vision changed her into a Stigmatic and she knew her mission, to dissect demons. She kidnapped the victim and interrogated them, using a God-Machine granted power that causes a temporary glitch to Demons she touches and keeps Demons from entering their Demon Form. Since her awakening she has been using her power to find Demons as well as dissect any Demons she finds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T13:13:26-07:00","id":1399126,"title":"","content":"Note: This one requires system knowledge of Mummy, which I only have a limited knowledge of.<br /> <br /> 6.<u><b> High Priest </b></u><u><b>Giacomo</b></u><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> - Long ago the God-Machine managed to subjugate an entire Mummy's Cult. Instead of converting the Cult to worship the God-Machine the Cult believes that the God-Machine is an aspect of their master. When the Mummy awakens the Cult uses G-M corrupted prophecies to direct the Mummy into attacking Demons as well as cull any loyalist cultists who have realized the cult has been compromised. Giacomo is a powerful piece of Infrastructure that has been crafted to direct the cult. Often times he will sit back and let events play out so as not to arouse suspicion. Usually the Mummy's memory of the Cult's corruption happens just before they fall back to rest. Allowing Giacomo to keep the game up for longer.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T09:34:21-07:00","id":1399306,"title":"","content":"I don't know if I have posted this elsewhere on the forum, but here's a link to a cryptid: <a href=\"https://kanka.io/en-US/campaign/12615/characters/162324\" target=\"_blank\">Hive Bears</a>.<br /> <br /> In my campaign I had a progression of antagonists: Cryptid -&gt; Cultists and Simulacra -&gt; single Demon opponent -&gt; Cult with Angelic supervision -&gt; Substantial Angelic activity. DtD is a little short on mid-level antagonists. <br /> <br /> I haven't thought enough about Stigmatics (especially Stigmatic Hunters) as antagonists. Some of your posted ideas would work great for shorter Chronicles!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T06:59:14-07:00","id":1400081,"title":"","content":"7. <u><b>Horror Movie Protagonist</b></u>- Rachael was your typical average girl, but the God-Machine implanted Infrastructure around her. From her perspective she's trapped in a Horror Movie. She can't stop moving or else the Horror Movie Antagonist will get her, a stereotypical serial killer or other horror movie antagonist. She's a reluctant hero and she has to feed the Antagonist to keep its bloodlust sated. Rachael will often find herself in dangerous situations and drag in innocent people in order to save herself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}